<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64571" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαίσων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>native cook</i>, at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.659a
			</span></i>; derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μασᾶσθαι</span> by
			Chrysipp.ibid., but acc. to Ar.Byz.ibid. it means <i>comic mask of
				a cook, sailor</i>, etc., named after an actor so
			called:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαισωνικὰ</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκώμματα</span>, ib.b.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
